Adventure:

Found a luckstone, so didn't go to bottom of mines. Hung around in
mines long enough to get protection money, then left.

Two magic lamps in mines' hardware store. Bought them both. One
blessed. Rubbed until I got a djinn, who said, "I'm free," and didn't
do anything else. So my large dog Fido snuffed him out. That's what
ingratitude will get you.

First scroll of ID ID'd all my stuff, so I was able to figure out
which potions were worth diluting down to water (most of them), did
that, so now I have a good supply of HW. Only thing I'm lacking is a
BoH. Continues to be a problem as I make my way down to Medusa. Also
have not come across any scrolls of enchant armor, so have to rely on
enchantments I've found. Also, no magic markers, no rings, wands, or
cloaks of invisibility, so I'm still visible. Ended up clearing out a
deep-level vault and leprachaun hall, so I was able to get 9 points of
intrinsic AC. Also got a wish from a throne; considered other options,
ended up choosing GDSM.

Found BoH on quest and /oInv, so those two problems were taken care
of. Had alchemized 10 bd!oFH before embarking on quest and quaffed 5.
Needed a few more in fighting Chromatic Dragon. Not so much for the
Dragon as for the monsters it summoned; nearly died after Chromatic
Dragon was already killed.

Found portal to Ludios and conquored it. Black dragon corpse gave
disintegration resistance. Donated the spoils to temple on dlvl 24,
6000 Z at a time. Got naked AC down to -1, which was good, because I
still haven't found ?oEA yet.

Down to Medusa, no means of crossing water, so I did the dig-down
come-back-up trick; this yielded boots of levitation. Was hoping for
water walking, so as to easily blank scrolls and dilute potions.

Cleared out Castle and had some tactical choices to make. Only piece
of AK I already have is GDSM. Found speed boots and gauntlets of
dexterity, which was good, because WoW was only at 0:1, and I hadn't
ID'd charging scrolls yet. (Also found cursed -1 GoP.) I did finally
find one ?oEA at the Castle, so I didn't have to wish for that too
before writing one. Still using dwarvish cloak (because I'd found it
at +3). Decided to get the priest of Moloch's robe from the Valley to
try to do some spellcasting; while working my way through the Valley
got level-drained down to 14, thus losing warning intrinsic. 

Got the robe, used altar to BUC ID potions, alchemized some !oFH and
!oGA, got Int up to 17, read all my spellbooks, and got three
spellbooks (wizard lock, cone of cold, cancellation) in non-restricted
categories. No wand of polymorph to try to polypile spellbooks. Almost
gave up on spellcasting, but did practice matter spells with wizard
lock spell, getting that up to basic. With only two wishes (plus final
one) left in wand, waiting a while before wishing for HoB.

Ended up finding another magic lamp on dlvl 48. Finally, a grateful
djinni! Wished for my HoB, and now I am able to spellcast. No good
attack spells except cone of cold, but that's a pretty good one to
have. Still no /oPoly and no =oTC. Probably have to travel up the
dungeon until I find a tengu. That's an important part of my ascension
run.

Never found that tengu or any other means of TC. Did find some more
spellbooks: dig, force bolt, and magic missile. Maxed out spellcasting
ability (basic in attack, skilled in matter) and decided to make my
run at the Wizard's Tower. A /oDeath took out Rodney with no problem,
and I got the Book. Had to work my way down to the VS (usually just
levelport) due to no TC. Used WoDeath on High Priest and got the
Amulet. Quaffed the !oGL I found in the Sanctum on a hunch, and rose
through the ceiling. This is what I usually do to avoid fighting my
way back out of the Sanctum, but I hadn't been able to find/make any
cursed !oGL to have with me at the crucial moment.

Really blew it on my way back up. Forgot to eat, and fainted in the
vicinity of a MMF. Had to helplessly scroll through several lines of
my brains getting sucked before I could eat a handy lump of royal
jelly and then pulverize the nasty beast. Wrote a lot of magic mapping
scrolls to get out of Gehennom and past Medusa. After that, I just
found my way out if I'd forgotten the level. Other than memory loss, I
was really lucky on my way back up. Rodney reappeared only four times,
once before I'd gotten to the Sanctum, so only three times on the way
back up, including the obligatory Plane of Earth appearance. Never
Double Troubled me or stole anything, and I don't think I ever
suffered a malignant aura. Got uneasy feelings and bunches of monsters
often.

Planes were uneventful. Teleported air elementals away; never got
engulfed. Materialized on Astral toward the left side, so I did left
first. Went toe to toe with Pestilence a couple of times; !oFH came in
handy. Left altar was Chaotic, so I went for the middle, which turned
out to be Neutral. One of my wands ended up hitting the High Priest of
Anhur, so he was attacking me as I offered the Amulet to his god.
Ungrateful wretch. He'd better not need any demigod favors.

